---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro'
import snapshot from '../../data/rich-snapshot.json'
import weak from '../../data/weak-passphrases.json'

const richCount = snapshot.entries.length
const richTotal = Math.round(snapshot.entries.reduce((sum, e) => sum + e.btc, 0))
---

<Base title="Just hack it">
  <article class="journey">
    <!-- Beat 0 — the doubt, and the reframe -->
    <section class="beat">
      <p class="doubt">
        “It’s just software. Software gets hacked every day. Someone, somewhere, will crack
        it eventually.”
      </p>
      <h1>Just hack it</h1>
      <p>
        There’s no company to break into. No password to reset. No admin door. Every Bitcoin
        wallet is locked by one thing: a <strong>private key</strong> — an enormous secret
        number. “Hacking” a wallet means exactly one thing: <strong>guessing that number.</strong>
      </p>
      <p>So let’s try. <a href="/fundamentals/">What’s a private key? →</a></p>
    </section>

    <!-- Beat 1 — make the lock -->
    <section class="beat">
      <h2>1. Make a key of your own</h2>
      <p>
        A key is just 256 coin flips — heads and tails, ones and zeros. Flip them and you’ve
        minted a real Bitcoin key, right here in your browser.
        <span class="trust">Nothing is sent anywhere. This never leaves your device.</span>
      </p>

      <button id="flip" class="big-orange">Flip 256 coins</button>

      <div id="mine" hidden>
        <p class="coins mono" id="coins"></p>
        <p class="field-label">Your private key (a real one):</p>
        <p id="key" class="mono key"></p>
        <p class="field-label">The vault addresses it unlocks:</p>
        <ul class="addresses mono" id="addresses"></ul>
        <p class="point">
          A fortune can be locked by 256 coin flips — and no one on Earth can ever flip the
          same sequence twice. This key is now yours. For the rest of this page, <em>you</em>
          are the wallet under attack.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Beat 2 — hire your attacker -->
    <section class="beat" id="scene-crack">
      <h2>2. Now try to guess someone else’s</h2>
      <p>
        Guessing a key means trying random numbers until one opens a funded wallet. Hire your
        hardware and let it run. Watch two things: how many keys you actually try, and how far
        the bar moves.
      </p>

      <div class="tiers" id="tiers"></div>
      <p class="basis" id="tier-basis"></p>

      <div class="crack-controls">
        <button id="crack" class="big-orange">Start cracking</button>
        <button id="stop" class="ghost" hidden>Stop and see the damage</button>
      </div>

      <div id="dash" hidden>
        <div class="counter">
          <span class="num mono" id="tried">0</span>
          <span class="counter-label">real keys tried in your browser</span>
        </div>

        <div class="bar-wrap">
          <div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill" id="bar"></div></div>
          <p class="bar-pct mono" id="pct"></p>
        </div>

        <p class="wait" id="wait"></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Beat 2.5 — the scale interlude -->
    <section class="beat scale" id="scale">
      <h2>Why the bar will never move</h2>
      <p>The number of possible keys is 2<sup>256</sup>. Lined up against everything we can count:</p>
      <ul class="ladder">
        <li>Grains of sand on Earth — about 10<sup>19</sup></li>
        <li>Stars in the observable universe — about 10<sup>24</sup></li>
        <li>Atoms in your body — about 10<sup>27</sup></li>
        <li>Atoms in the whole Earth — about 10<sup>50</sup></li>
        <li class="win">Possible Bitcoin keys — about 10<sup>77</sup></li>
        <li>Atoms in the observable universe — about 10<sup>80</sup></li>
      </ul>
      <p class="point">
        There are nearly as many possible keys as there are atoms in the universe. Picking a
        funded one at random isn’t hard — it’s not <em>possible</em> in any span of time that
        means anything.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Beat 3 — the turn -->
    <section class="beat turn" id="turn" hidden>
      <h2>3. The knife was real</h2>
      <p>
        Every key you just tried was a genuine Bitcoin key. If any one of them had matched a
        funded wallet, those coins would have been yours. You checked each against a real
        snapshot of the <strong>{richCount} richest wallets on the network</strong> — together
        holding about {richTotal.toLocaleString()} BTC.
      </p>
      <p class="verdict mono" id="turn-verdict"></p>
      <p class="point">
        Not a metaphor. You attacked Bitcoin with a real weapon, and it did nothing at all.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Beat 4 — the honest footnote -->
    <section class="beat">
      <h2>4. But people <em>do</em> get hacked — here’s the truth</h2>
      <p>
        Nobody has ever guessed a properly made key. Bitcoin is lost when keys are
        <strong>stolen from where humans keep them</strong> — exchange breaches, phishing,
        malware. The maths holds; the buildings around it leak. The vault has never been
        picked. People get robbed in the car park.
      </p>

      <details class="footnote">
        <summary>See the one time the maths does break: a human-chosen key</summary>
        <div class="footnote-body">
          <p>
            Instead of 256 coin flips, some people locked their coins with a <em>passphrase</em>
            they could remember — a “brain wallet.” But a passphrase is a single guess, not
            2<sup>256</sup>. Type one and watch its key appear <strong>instantly</strong>:
          </p>
          <div class="passphrase-row">
            <input id="phrase" type="text" placeholder="type any passphrase…" autocomplete="off" />
            <button id="crackphrase" class="big-orange small">Crack it</button>
          </div>
          <p class="suggest">
            Try one:
            <span id="suggestions"></span>
          </p>
          <div id="phrase-out" hidden>
            <p class="field-label">Cracked in one step. The address it produces:</p>
            <p id="phrase-address" class="mono key"></p>
            <p id="phrase-time" class="verdict mono"></p>
          </div>
          <p class="src">
            {weak.note}
            <br />Source: <a href={weak.sourceUrl} rel="noopener">{weak.source}</a> · dataset dated {weak.retrieved}.
          </p>
          <p class="point">
            Same maths, opposite outcome. The coin flips <em>are</em> the security. Never let a
            human pick.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </section>

    <!-- Beat 5 — the door -->
    <section class="beat door">
      <p class="door-line">
        So you can’t pick the lock. Fine — forget the lock. Find the building it lives in and
        burn it down.
      </p>
      <a href="/attack/shut-down/" class="cta">Attack 2: Shut down the server →</a>
    </section>

    <p class="src foot-src">
      Rich-list snapshot: <a href={snapshot.sourceUrl} rel="noopener">{snapshot.source}</a> ·
      dated {snapshot.retrieved}. Hardware speeds are generous estimates, labelled as such.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<script>
  import {
    checkAgainstSnapshot,
    flipsToPrivateKey,
    keyToHex,
    passphraseToPrivateKey,
    privateKeyToAddresses,
    randomFlips,
    randomPrivateKey,
    type DerivedAddresses,
    type RichSnapshot,
  } from '../../engines/hack/engine'
  import {
    TIERS,
    describeWait,
    fractionSearched,
    formatScientific,
  } from '../../engines/hack/cracker'
  import snapshotJson from '../../data/rich-snapshot.json'
  import weakJson from '../../data/weak-passphrases.json'
  import { browserStorage, markAttempted } from '../../progress/progress'

  const snapshot = snapshotJson as RichSnapshot
  const $ = (id: string) => document.getElementById(id)!

  // ---- Beat 1: mint the visitor's own key ----
  $('flip').addEventListener('click', () => {
    let flips = randomFlips()
    let key: Uint8Array | null = null
    while (key === null) {
      try {
        key = flipsToPrivateKey(flips)
      } catch {
        flips = randomFlips()
      }
    }
    const addr = privateKeyToAddresses(key)
    $('coins').textContent = flips.map((f) => (f ? 'H' : 'T')).join('')
    $('key').textContent = keyToHex(key)
    $('addresses').innerHTML = [
      `<li><span class="tag">legacy</span> ${addr.legacy}</li>`,
      `<li><span class="tag">3-address</span> ${addr.nested}</li>`,
      `<li><span class="tag">bc1</span> ${addr.native}</li>`,
    ].join('')
    ;($('mine') as HTMLElement).hidden = false
  })

  // ---- Beat 2: hire a tier ----
  let tierIndex = 0
  const tiersEl = $('tiers')
  TIERS.forEach((tier, i) => {
    const b = document.createElement('button')
    b.className = 'tier' + (i === 0 ? ' on' : '')
    b.textContent = tier.name
    b.addEventListener('click', () => {
      tierIndex = i
      ;[...tiersEl.children].forEach((c, ci) => c.classList.toggle('on', ci === i))
      $('tier-basis').textContent = 'Estimate: ' + tier.basis + '.'
      updateWait()
    })
    tiersEl.appendChild(b)
  })
  $('tier-basis').textContent = 'Estimate: ' + TIERS[0].basis + '.'

  // ---- Beat 2: the cracking loop (real keys, real checks) ----
  let running = false
  let tried = 0
  let hit: { label: string } | null = null

  function updateWait() {
    $('wait').textContent = describeWait(TIERS[tierIndex].keysPerSecond)
  }

  function render() {
    ;($('tried') as HTMLElement).textContent = tried.toLocaleString()
    const frac = fractionSearched(tried)
    // The bar is honest: a fraction this small rounds to a flat zero width.
    ;($('bar') as HTMLElement).style.width = Math.min(100, frac * 100) + '%'
    $('pct').textContent = frac === 0 ? '0%' : formatScientific(frac * 100) + ' %'
  }

  function loop() {
    if (!running) return
    // A real batch: mint random keys, derive every address shape, check the list.
    for (let i = 0; i < 400; i++) {
      const addresses: DerivedAddresses = privateKeyToAddresses(randomPrivateKey())
      const match = checkAgainstSnapshot(addresses, snapshot)
      tried++
      if (match) {
        hit = match
        running = false
        break
      }
    }
    render()
    if (running) requestAnimationFrame(loop)
    else if (hit) reveal()
  }

  $('crack').addEventListener('click', () => {
    running = true
    hit = null
    ;($('dash') as HTMLElement).hidden = false
    ;($('crack') as HTMLElement).hidden = true
    ;($('stop') as HTMLElement).hidden = false
    updateWait()
    requestAnimationFrame(loop)
  })

  $('stop').addEventListener('click', () => {
    running = false
    reveal()
  })

  function reveal() {
    ;($('crack') as HTMLElement).hidden = false
    ;($('stop') as HTMLElement).hidden = true
    const turn = $('turn') as HTMLElement
    turn.hidden = false
    $('turn-verdict').textContent = hit
      ? `IMPOSSIBLE-ODDS HIT: one of your ${tried.toLocaleString()} keys opened “${hit.label}”. You are the luckiest being in the history of the universe.`
      : `You tried ${tried.toLocaleString()} real keys. Matches against ${snapshot.entries.length.toLocaleString()} funded wallets: ZERO. Nothing to steal.`
    // Stamp the campaign: this attack was run, and the network held.
    markAttempted(browserStorage(), 'hack')
    turn.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' })
  }

  // ---- Beat 4: the passphrase footnote ----
  const phraseInput = $('phrase') as HTMLInputElement
  const sugg = $('suggestions')
  ;(weakJson.suggestions as string[]).forEach((s) => {
    const chip = document.createElement('button')
    chip.className = 'chip'
    chip.textContent = s
    chip.addEventListener('click', () => {
      phraseInput.value = s
      crackPhrase()
    })
    sugg.appendChild(chip)
  })

  function crackPhrase() {
    const phrase = phraseInput.value
    if (!phrase) return
    let key: Uint8Array
    try {
      key = passphraseToPrivateKey(phrase)
    } catch {
      $('phrase-time').textContent = 'That phrase produced an invalid key — try another.'
      ;($('phrase-out') as HTMLElement).hidden = false
      return
    }
    const addr = privateKeyToAddresses(key)
    $('phrase-address').textContent = addr.legacy
    $('phrase-time').textContent =
      'Time to derive it: one SHA-256 — under a millisecond. A machine tried this exact phrase years ago.'
    ;($('phrase-out') as HTMLElement).hidden = false
  }

  $('crackphrase').addEventListener('click', crackPhrase)
  phraseInput.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
    if ((e as KeyboardEvent).key === 'Enter') crackPhrase()
  })
</script>

<style>
  .journey {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 3.5rem;
  }
  .beat {
    scroll-margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }
  .doubt {
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--dim);
    border-left: 3px solid #2a3140;
    padding-left: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }
  .trust {
    display: block;
    color: var(--orange);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin-top: 0.4rem;
  }
  .big-orange {
    background: var(--orange);
    color: #0a0a0a;
    border: none;
    border-radius: 8px;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    padding: 0.9rem 2rem;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .big-orange.small {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    padding: 0.6rem 1.1rem;
  }
  .ghost {
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--text);
    border: 1px solid #2a3140;
    border-radius: 8px;
    font-size: 1rem;
    padding: 0.9rem 1.5rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    margin-left: 0.75rem;
  }
  .mono {
    font-family: ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace;
    word-break: break-all;
  }
  .field-label {
    color: var(--dim);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.2rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }
  .key,
  .addresses {
    background: var(--panel);
    padding: 0.6rem 0.8rem;
    border-radius: 6px;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }
  .coins {
    color: var(--dim);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
    max-height: 3.5rem;
    overflow: hidden;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
  }
  .addresses {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0.8rem;
    margin: 0.2rem 0 0;
  }
  .addresses li {
    padding: 0.15rem 0;
  }
  .tag {
    display: inline-block;
    min-width: 5.5rem;
    color: var(--orange);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }
  .point {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }
  .tiers {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    margin: 1rem 0 0.5rem;
  }
  .tier {
    background: var(--panel);
    color: var(--dim);
    border: 1px solid #2a3140;
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 0.5rem 1rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .tier.on {
    color: #0a0a0a;
    background: var(--orange);
    border-color: var(--orange);
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .basis {
    color: var(--dim);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    min-height: 1.2rem;
  }
  .crack-controls {
    margin: 1rem 0;
  }
  .counter {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    margin: 1.25rem 0;
  }
  .counter .num {
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--orange);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .counter-label {
    color: var(--dim);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
  .bar-wrap {
    margin: 1rem 0;
  }
  .bar-track {
    height: 14px;
    background: var(--panel);
    border: 1px solid #2a3140;
    border-radius: 999px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .bar-fill {
    height: 100%;
    width: 0;
    background: var(--orange);
  }
  .bar-pct {
    color: var(--dim);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    margin-top: 0.4rem;
  }
  .wait {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .scale .ladder {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.4rem;
  }
  .scale .ladder li {
    background: var(--panel);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 0.6rem 0.9rem;
  }
  .scale .ladder .win {
    background: #2a1c07;
    border: 1px solid var(--orange);
    color: var(--orange);
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .turn {
    border: 1px solid var(--orange);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    background: #140f06;
  }
  .verdict {
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    margin: 1rem 0;
  }
  .footnote {
    background: var(--panel);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 0.5rem 1rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }
  .footnote summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    color: var(--orange);
    padding: 0.5rem 0;
  }
  .footnote-body {
    padding-top: 0.5rem;
  }
  .passphrase-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    margin: 0.75rem 0;
  }
  .passphrase-row input {
    flex: 1 1 14rem;
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid #2a3140;
    border-radius: 8px;
    color: var(--text);
    padding: 0.6rem 0.9rem;
    font-size: 1rem;
  }
  .suggest {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--dim);
  }
  .chip {
    background: transparent;
    border: 1px solid #2a3140;
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: var(--text);
    padding: 0.25rem 0.7rem;
    margin: 0.15rem;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .src {
    color: var(--dim);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .foot-src {
    border-top: 1px solid #1c212b;
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }
  .door {
    text-align: center;
  }
  .door-line {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-style: italic;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }
</style>
